<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banjarmasin War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a>–<a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Banjar War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjarmasin">Banjarmasin</a> War was a conflict in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial government and supporters of the Banjar Sultanate, beginning in 1859 after the Dutch imposed their own candidate in a succession dispute following <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Adam's death. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pangeran-antasari">Pangeran Antasari</a>, the resistance attacked Dutch posts and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mines. The Dutch abolished the sultanate in 1860, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> fighting continued until 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banjarmasin-war.jpg" alt="Banjarmasin War" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: W.A. van Rees · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1._ZM_Stoomschip_Celebes_in_gevecht_met_een_Kota_Mara_6_aug_1859_Poeloe_Kananat_opgenomen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
